<phyphox version="1.7" locale="en" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Magnetic Field</title>
    <category>Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense</category>
    <description>Plots the local magnetic field vector measured by the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense's LSM9DS1 IMU; nearby metal, currents, and calibration affect the result.</description>
    <link label="Find more">https://vulgarisation.fr/?lang=en</link>
  <icon format="base64"></icon>
	<color>009297</color> 
    <translations>
        <translation locale="fr">
            <title>Champ magnétique</title>
            <category>Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense</category>
            <description>Trace le vecteur du champ magnétique local mesuré par l'IMU LSM9DS1 du Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense ; le métal proche, les courants et la calibration influencent le résultat.</description>
            <link label="Plus d'infos">https://vulgarisation.fr/</link>
            <string original="Magnetometer x">champ magnétique selon x</string>
            <string original="Magnetometer y">champ magnétique selon y</string>
            <string original="Magnetometer z">champ magnétique selon z</string>
            <string original="Magnetometer">champ magnétique</string>
            <string original="Absolute magnetic field">Norme du champ magnétique</string>
            <string original="time">temps</string>
            <string original="Magnetic field">Champ magnétique</string>
            <string original="Absolute">Norme</string>
            <string original="Simple">Composantes</string>
        <string original="Calibration">Étalonnage</string>
<string original="Bias x">Biais x</string>
<string original="Gain x">Facteur x</string>
<string original="Bias y">Biais y</string>
<string original="Gain y">Facteur y</string>
<string original="Bias z">Biais z</string>
<string original="Gain z">Facteur z</string>
<string original="Setup">Montage</string>
<string original="Use a nonmagnetic mount away from steel, magnets, power cables and changing currents. Rotate the complete assembly through many orientations at one location. Axis bias and gain provide only a diagonal correction; soft-iron coupling and misalignment require a full matrix calibration outside this view. Preserve missing readings as gaps. A field direction is not a compass heading without tilt and local-field corrections.">Utiliser un support non magnétique loin de l’acier, des aimants, des câbles et des courants variables. Tourner tout le montage dans de nombreuses orientations au même endroit. Biais et facteurs par axe ne donnent qu’une correction diagonale ; les couplages et désalignements nécessitent un étalonnage matriciel externe. Garder les lacunes des mesures manquantes. Une direction de champ ne donne pas un cap sans correction de l’inclinaison et du champ local.</string>
<string original="Record a stable reference before and after each trial. The BLE interval is at least 50 ms; unavailable sensor readings remain NaN. Fast signals need an independently verified bandwidth and anti-alias filtering.">Enregistrer une référence stable avant et après chaque essai. L’intervalle BLE est d’au moins 50 ms ; les mesures indisponibles restent NaN. Les signaux rapides nécessitent une bande passante vérifiée et un filtre anti-repliement.</string>
<string original="Enter coefficients measured on this apparatus. Defaults are nominal, not a calibration. Changing a coefficient recalculates the entire trace; original readings and settings are exported separately. Clearing data restores the defaults.">Saisir les coefficients mesurés sur ce montage. Les valeurs initiales sont nominales, sans étalonnage. Un changement recalcule toute la courbe ; mesures originales et réglages sont exportés séparément. Effacer les données rétablit les valeurs initiales.</string>
        </translation>
        <translation locale="de">
            <title>Magnetfeld</title>
            <category>Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense</category>
            <description>Das lokale Magnetfeld mit dem LSM9DS1-IMU des Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense messen; nahe Metallteile, Ströme und die Kalibrierung beeinflussen das Ergebnis.</description>
            <link label="Weitere Informationen (englisch)">https://vulgarisation.fr/?lang=en</link>
            <string original="Magnetometer x">Magnetometer x</string>
            <string original="Magnetometer y">Magnetometer y</string>
            <string original="Magnetometer z">Magnetometer z</string>
            <string original="Magnetometer">Magnetometer</string>
            <string original="Absolute magnetic field">Betrag des Magnetfelds</string>
            <string original="time">Zeit</string>
            <string original="Magnetic field">Magnetfeld</string>
            <string original="Absolute">Betrag</string>
            <string original="Simple">Einfach</string>
        <string original="Calibration">Kalibrierung</string>
<string original="Bias x">Offset x</string>
<string original="Gain x">Faktor x</string>
<string original="Bias y">Offset y</string>
<string original="Gain y">Faktor y</string>
<string original="Bias z">Offset z</string>
<string original="Gain z">Faktor z</string>
<string original="Setup">Aufbau</string>
<string original="Use a nonmagnetic mount away from steel, magnets, power cables and changing currents. Rotate the complete assembly through many orientations at one location. Axis bias and gain provide only a diagonal correction; soft-iron coupling and misalignment require a full matrix calibration outside this view. Preserve missing readings as gaps. A field direction is not a compass heading without tilt and local-field corrections.">Eine nichtmagnetische Halterung fern von Stahl, Magneten, Stromkabeln und wechselnden Strömen verwenden. Den gesamten Aufbau am selben Ort in viele Richtungen drehen. Achsenoffset und Faktor liefern nur eine diagonale Korrektur; Weicheisenkopplung und Fehlorientierung benötigen eine vollständige Matrixkalibrierung außerhalb dieser Ansicht. Fehlende Werte bleiben Lücken. Die Feldrichtung ist ohne Neigungs- und lokale Feldkorrekturen kein Kompasskurs.</string>
<string original="Record a stable reference before and after each trial. The BLE interval is at least 50 ms; unavailable sensor readings remain NaN. Fast signals need an independently verified bandwidth and anti-alias filtering.">Vor und nach jedem Versuch eine stabile Referenz aufzeichnen. Das BLE-Intervall beträgt mindestens 50 ms; nicht verfügbare Sensormesswerte bleiben NaN. Schnelle Signale benötigen eine unabhängig geprüfte Bandbreite und einen Anti-Aliasing-Filter.</string>
<string original="Enter coefficients measured on this apparatus. Defaults are nominal, not a calibration. Changing a coefficient recalculates the entire trace; original readings and settings are exported separately. Clearing data restores the defaults.">Am eigenen Aufbau gemessene Koeffizienten eingeben. Vorgaben sind Nennwerte, keine Kalibrierung. Änderungen berechnen die gesamte Kurve neu; ursprüngliche Messwerte und Einstellungen werden getrennt exportiert. Daten löschen setzt die Vorgaben zurück.</string>
        </translation>
    </translations>
    <data-containers>
	    <xi:include href="includes/containers_ch0_ch5.xml" xpointer="xpointer(/containers/node())" />
    <container size="1" init="0">bias_x</container>
<container size="1" init="1">gain_x</container>
<container size="0">CH2_cal</container>
<container size="1" init="0">bias_y</container>
<container size="1" init="1">gain_y</container>
<container size="0">CH3_cal</container>
<container size="1" init="0">bias_z</container>
<container size="1" init="1">gain_z</container>
<container size="0">CH4_cal</container>
<container size="0">CH5_cal</container>
    </data-containers>
    <input>
        <bluetooth mode="notification" rate="1" subscribeOnStart="false" id="Sense">
            <xi:include href="includes/bluetooth_outputs_ch1_ch5.xml" xpointer="xpointer(/outputs/node())" />
        </bluetooth>
    </input>
    <output>
        <bluetooth id="Sense">
            <config char="cddf1003-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="float32LittleEndian">3.0</config>
        </bluetooth>
    </output>
    <views>
        <view label="Graph">
            <graph label="Magnetometer x" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="green" partialUpdate="false" labelX="time" labelY="B" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="µT" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH2_cal</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Magnetometer y" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="blue" partialUpdate="false" labelX="time" labelY="B" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="µT" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH3_cal</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Magnetometer z" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="yellow" partialUpdate="false" labelX="time" labelY="B" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="µT" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH4_cal</input>
            </graph>
        </view>
        
        <view label="Absolute">
            <graph label="Absolute magnetic field" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="white" partialUpdate="false" labelX="time" labelY="B" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="µT" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH5_cal</input>
            </graph>
            <value label="Absolute magnetic field" size="2" precision="3" unit="µT" color="white">
                <input>CH5_cal</input>
            </value>
        </view>
        
        <view label="Multi">
            <graph label="Magnetic field" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" partialUpdate="false" labelX="t" labelY="B" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="µT" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x" color="green">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH2_cal</input>
                <input axis="x" color="blue">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH3_cal</input>
                <input axis="x" color="yellow">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH4_cal</input>
                <input axis="x" color="white">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH5_cal</input>
            </graph>
            <value label="Magnetometer x" size="2" precision="2" unit="µT" color="green">
                <input>CH2_cal</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Magnetometer y" size="2" precision="2" unit="µT" color="blue">
                <input>CH3_cal</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Magnetometer z" size="2" precision="2" unit="µT" color="yellow">
                <input>CH4_cal</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Absolute magnetic field" size="2" precision="2" unit="µT" color="white">
                <input>CH5_cal</input>
            </value>
        </view>
        
         <view label="Simple">
            <value label="Magnetometer x" size="2" precision="2" unit="µT" color="green">
                <input>CH2_cal</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Magnetometer y" size="2" precision="2" unit="µT" color="blue">
                <input>CH3_cal</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Magnetometer z" size="2" precision="2" unit="µT" color="yellow">
                <input>CH4_cal</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Absolute magnetic field" size="2" precision="2" unit="µT" color="white">
                <input>CH5_cal</input>
            </value>
        </view>
    <view label="Setup">
    <info label="Use a nonmagnetic mount away from steel, magnets, power cables and changing currents. Rotate the complete assembly through many orientations at one location. Axis bias and gain provide only a diagonal correction; soft-iron coupling and misalignment require a full matrix calibration outside this view. Preserve missing readings as gaps. A field direction is not a compass heading without tilt and local-field corrections." />
    <info label="Record a stable reference before and after each trial. The BLE interval is at least 50 ms; unavailable sensor readings remain NaN. Fast signals need an independently verified bandwidth and anti-alias filtering." />
</view>
    <view label="Calibration">
    <info label="Enter coefficients measured on this apparatus. Defaults are nominal, not a calibration. Changing a coefficient recalculates the entire trace; original readings and settings are exported separately. Clearing data restores the defaults." />
    <edit label="Bias x" unit="µT" default="0" decimal="true" signed="true">
        <output>bias_x</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Gain x" unit="" default="1" decimal="true" signed="false" min="0.000000001">
        <output>gain_x</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Bias y" unit="µT" default="0" decimal="true" signed="true">
        <output>bias_y</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Gain y" unit="" default="1" decimal="true" signed="false" min="0.000000001">
        <output>gain_y</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Bias z" unit="µT" default="0" decimal="true" signed="true">
        <output>bias_z</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Gain z" unit="" default="1" decimal="true" signed="false" min="0.000000001">
        <output>gain_z</output>
    </edit>
</view>
    </views>
    <analysis sleep="0.05">
    <formula formula="([1_]-[2])*[3]">
        <input clear="false">CH2</input>
        <input clear="false">bias_x</input>
        <input clear="false">gain_x</input>
        <output clear="true">CH2_cal</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="([1_]-[2])*[3]">
        <input clear="false">CH3</input>
        <input clear="false">bias_y</input>
        <input clear="false">gain_y</input>
        <output clear="true">CH3_cal</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="([1_]-[2])*[3]">
        <input clear="false">CH4</input>
        <input clear="false">bias_z</input>
        <input clear="false">gain_z</input>
        <output clear="true">CH4_cal</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="sqrt([1_]^2+[2_]^2+[3_]^2)">
        <input clear="false">CH2_cal</input>
        <input clear="false">CH3_cal</input>
        <input clear="false">CH4_cal</input>
        <output clear="true">CH5_cal</output>
    </formula>
</analysis>
    <export>
        <set name="Raw data (µT)">
            <data name="Time t (s)">CH1</data>
            <data name="Magnetometer x (µT)">CH2</data>
            <data name="Magnetometer y (µT)">CH3</data>
            <data name="Magnetometer z (µT)">CH4</data>
            <data name="Absolute magnetic field (µT)">CH5</data>
        </set>
    <set name="Calibrated field (µT)">
    <data name="Time t (s)">CH1</data>
    <data name="Magnetic field x (µT)">CH2_cal</data>
    <data name="Magnetic field y (µT)">CH3_cal</data>
    <data name="Magnetic field z (µT)">CH4_cal</data>
    <data name="Magnetic field magnitude (µT)">CH5_cal</data>
</set>
    <set name="Calibration settings">
    <data name="Bias x (µT)">bias_x</data>
    <data name="Gain x">gain_x</data>
    <data name="Bias y (µT)">bias_y</data>
    <data name="Gain y">gain_y</data>
    <data name="Bias z (µT)">bias_z</data>
    <data name="Gain z">gain_z</data>
</set>
    <set name="Timing">
    <data name="Device time (s)">CH1</data>
    <data name="BLE receive time (s)">CH0</data>
</set>
    </export>
</phyphox>
